  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The blessed land is small at the bottom and larger higher up: it has little land, but the higher in the air one goes, the larger the space. A sky that greatly exceeds ordinary blessed lands holds countless circular wooden eagle nests floating like small hills, with innumerable iron eagles resting in them; when groups fly in formation the view is spectacular.",
      "chapters": [
        691
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a garden pavilion at the highest part of the land, four Hei tribe supreme elders sit around a square stone table under a heavy atmosphere. Countless circular wooden eagle nests float in the sky, with innumerable iron eagles resting in them. Hei Cheng rises into the pavilion and returns Dark Prison after suppressing Qiao tribe.",
      "chapters": [
        691
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "eagle-nests-and-sky-space",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_hei_tribe",
        "char_hei_cheng",
        "house_dark_prison",
        "fac_qiao_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Like Dong Fang tribe’s Jade Pool, Murong tribe’s Yin-Yang, and Guan tribe’s Shi Huang, Hei tribe’s Iron Eagle blessed land is a main camp pieced together from contributions by various Gu Immortals. Most super forces in the five regions build headquarters that way.",
      "chapters": [
        795
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "pieced-headquarters",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_dong_fang_tribe",
        "fac_murong_tribe",
        "fac_guan_tribe",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Iron Eagle blessed land was Hei tribe’s headquarters originally. After that tribe is wiped out, Heavenly Lord Bai Zu takes it over as Bai Zu tribe’s main base, and for a time the land is hidden in empty space so it cannot be seen from outside.",
      "chapters": [
        1169
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ownership-change",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_heavenly_lord_bai_zu",
        "fac_bai_zu_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Under Bai Zu control it has operated only a short time and remains far from Hei tribe’s prime. Ground resources are few, while the sky holds at least a hundred eagle nests; Bai Zu tribe pushes that specialty by raising iron crown eagles and other desolate beasts.",
      "chapters": [
        1170
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ownership-change",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan attacks Iron Eagle blessed land and loots more than eighty eagle nests from it, which he keeps floating in his Mini Purple Heaven.",
      "chapters": [
        1291
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "looted-by-fang-yuan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_mini_purple_heaven"
      ]
    }
  ],
